# 22. Pentesting vs Vulnerability Scanning

| Pentesting | Vulnerability Scanning |
|---|---|
| Human-guided | Often automated |
| Validates vulnerabilities | Identifies potential vulnerabilities |
| May involve controlled exploitation | Usually does not exploit |
| Determines real-world impact | Produces findings |
| Requires careful scope | Also requires authorization |

---

# 23. Pentesting vs Red Teaming

### Pentest

Usually focuses on identifying and validating vulnerabilities.

### Red Team

Usually simulates adversary behavior against broader objectives.

```text
Pentest
→ Find and validate weaknesses

Red Team
→ Simulate realistic adversary objectives
```

---

# 24. Common Mistakes

Avoid:

- Testing without authorization
- Ignoring scope
- Excessive exploitation
- Collecting unnecessary sensitive data
- Leaving persistence behind
- Failing to document evidence
- Ignoring cleanup
- Reporting vulnerabilities without remediation guidance

